s and new (anti-) steroidal agents: modulation of estrogen receptor activity by estrogens and anti-estrogens</article-title><source>J Steroid Biochem Mol Biol</source><year>1990</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>747</fpage><lpage>751</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2285586</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0960-0760(90)90415-H</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lippman</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Dickson</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Kasid</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gelmann</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Davidson</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>McManaway</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Huff</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bronzert</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bates</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Swain</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Autocrine and paracrine growth regulation of human breast cancer</article-title><source>J Steroid Biochem</source><year>1986</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>147</fpage><lpage>154</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3486321</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0022-4731(86)90044-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bates</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Davidson</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name><name><surname>Valverius</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Freter</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Dickson</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Tam</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Kudlow</surname><given-names>JE</gi